1
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:12,920
Brighten up and try stepping away,
won't you?

2
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:28,620
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out.

3
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand.

4
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,420
Hey, that strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:47,700
So, on the arcade's tiles,

6
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:56,300 --> 00:01:01,640
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

8
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:09,080
Pompous-faced politicians and
blue-eyeshadowed aunties too.

9
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:14,660
Go on, turn around that corner.

10
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:19,880
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

11
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:27,800
There's Kame-ari surely Kame-ari is there

12
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:32,940
Come on over, everyone, to our town

13
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:34,580
Thank you

14
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:40,620
The Honda Family Clan 2: Eve's Treasure

15
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:46,280
Ryo-chan, Ryo-chan, Ryo-chan

16
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:51,420
We're about to go to bed.

17
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:53,900
Honda-san came all this way to visit us.

18
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:57,540
It's fine.
I just stopped by briefly on my patrol.

19
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:01,900
It's not fine. We're on duty right now.

20
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:04,520
Reiko-san, what are you...

21
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:05,940
Just a little punishment.

22
00:02:06,940 --> 00:02:07,340
How's that?

23
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:13,520
There was a character like this in old anime,
wasn't there?

24
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:14,820
Eyelids too.

25
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:21,440
Ahahaha.

26
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:23,900
Reiko-san,
you've got a good sense of comedy.

27
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,420
Ahahaha.

28
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:26,380
Mm...

29
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:27,520
Mm...

30
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:31,240
I slept well.

31
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:34,160
What's with you lot gathering around?

32
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:35,780
You're here?

33
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:37,960
Honda, hey -

34
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,600
Mm...

35
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:41,820
What's with that weird face?

36
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:43,780
No way...

37
00:02:43,780 --> 00:02:44,720
Don't tell me the Chief's here?

38
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:47,520
No, no, it's not that.

39
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:49,960
Then what's with that face?

40
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:52,500
Yeah, well, this face isn't really a face -

41
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,080
Is Big Brother here?

42
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:56,180
That voice...

43
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:00,820
Monkey, why are you here?

44
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:04,420
I called first,
and they said you'd probably be here.

45
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:05,480
That girl...

46
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:07,240
This is Honda's little brother, Monkey.

47
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:09,020
A girl who looks that scary...

48
00:03:09,020 --> 00:03:13,900
She changes personality
when she rides a bike.

49
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:15,860
You're Honda's younger brother, right?

50
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:17,120
What happened, Monkey?

51
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:20,320
Big sis collapsed.

52
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:22,440
Eve...

53
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:30,380
Eve's your little sister,
the really shy one, right?

54
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:30,680
Yeah.

55
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:33,940
She wasn't exactly strong
to begin with, but...

56
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:35,980
I never thought she'd collapse.

57
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:39,460
Coming through!

58
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:43,280
I'm taking a shortcut.

59
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:00,260
Aaaaaaah

60
00:04:00,260 --> 00:04:00,720
Aaaaaaah

61
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:01,460
Aaaaaaah

62
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:02,180
Aaaaaaah

63
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:02,760
Aaaaaaah

64
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:02,900
Aaaaaaah

65
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:03,080
Aaaaaaah

66
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:03,740
Aaaaaaah

67
00:04:03,740 --> 00:04:13,720
Aaaaaaah

68
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:18,480
I just can't sit still.

69
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:21,000
I'm worried, I'm worried.

70
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:21,900
I'm worried.

71
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:29,320
I'm worried.

72
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:32,140
You're the one who's far more worrying.

73
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,440
Oh right, wasn't Honda's old man

74
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:36,640
Found it, here it is.

75
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:40,540
Put this on and pull yourself together.

76
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:43,160
Eve's sick, you know!

77
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:44,780
This isn't the time to
be keeping the shop open.

78
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,920
You don't need to open the shop,
just come along.

79
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:48,860
Right.

80
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:57,500
Hayato! What do you think
you're doing with your work?

81
00:04:57,880 --> 00:05:00,320
But Eve collapsed, so I...

82
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:02,480
People collapse sometimes
when they're alive.

83
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:05,120
Don't come running back over
every little thing like that.

84
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:08,020
Grown men pacing around
together won't cure anything.

85
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:09,700
Rather, get back to work.

86
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:11,780
What a difference from before.

87
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:13,320
As expected of the head
of the Honda household.

88
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:22,720
Big brother.

89
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,920
She got tired and caught a cold, Eve.

90
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:27,840
I'm sorry for worrying you.

91
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:30,160
Long time no see.

92
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:35,960
This is Ryo-san, big brother's senior.

93
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:37,460
You've met before, right?

94
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:42,400
You're as shy around people as ever

95
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:45,400
It's me, it's me.
Don't you recognize this face?

96
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:50,040
Don't make that kind of noise.

97
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:52,300
Senior's face!

98
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:54,220
What's wrong with my face?

99
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:56,980
Waaaaaaaah!

100
00:05:58,500 --> 00:05:59,820
You crazy bastard!

101
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:01,780
No, no, it wasn't me!

102
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:03,520
Reiko did it!

103
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:05,380
Why is this here?

104
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:07,720
Shut up, you're gonna kill me!

105
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:11,880
I'm back.

106
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:15,720
So you finally got through?

107
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:17,740
Eve finally seems to have fallen asleep.

108
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:21,580
Your sister got into university?

109
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:24,360
Yeah, she's a first-year student now.

110
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:29,460
Maybe the commute to university was too
much for her and that's why she collapsed.

111
00:06:29,460 --> 00:06:31,260
Isn't it a university in Tokyo?

112
00:06:31,260 --> 00:06:34,460
It's technically in Tokyo,
but it's quite far.

113
00:06:34,460 --> 00:06:37,060
The commute takes three hours one way.

114
00:06:37,060 --> 00:06:37,860
What?

115
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:40,180
It's out in Hachioji, though.

116
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:45,000
First the Joban Line from Minami-Senju,

117
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:47,060
then the Yamanote Line,

118
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:50,000
then transferring to the Chuo Line,

119
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:57,520
and then an hour by bus from the station.

120
00:07:08,980 --> 00:07:11,080
Six hours round trip

121
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:13,580
That's as long as Chief Teraiya's commute.

122
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:15,380
Doesn't the university
have a dorm or something?

123
00:07:15,380 --> 00:07:18,280
Apparently there's one a
little ways away, though.

124
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:20,580
She doesn't seem to want to leave home.

125
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:23,560
Well, she's a girl who's this shy around people,
after all.

126
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:25,100
I'm home.

127
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:26,840
It's Mom.

128
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:28,720
So you're Ryo-san?

129
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:31,120
I've heard all sorts of
things about you already.

130
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:33,080
I wonder what the rumors are.

131
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:34,400
Honda-kun.

132
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:36,580
Ryo-san.

133
00:07:36,580 --> 00:07:38,460
You'll stay for dinner too, won't you?

134
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:41,740
I'd never let a guest go
home without feeding him.

135
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:43,340
Well, that would be a
disgrace to the family name.

136
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:46,020
Alright, I'll make it right away.

137
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:48,700
Hey.

138
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:51,940
What does it take to change
your mother's personality?

139
00:07:51,940 --> 00:07:54,380
Mom's just a perfectly normal mom.

140
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:59,180
Your whole family changes personality when they ride a bike or put on a jumpsuit,
don't they?

141
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:03,560
Doesn't your mother turn savage when
she wears a kappogi or something?

142
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:04,840
That's not...

143
00:08:08,380 --> 00:08:10,220
Just as I thought.

144
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:14,100
I cut my finger with the kitchen knife.

145
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:15,740
Oops, oops.

146
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:19,380
Eve always leaves it to me,
so I hardly ever cook myself.

147
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:21,900
So she didn't turn violent after all.

148
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:23,480
What a troublesome mother.

149
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:25,200
That's why I said she was normal, didn't I?

150
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:29,220
Sorry to keep you waiting.

151
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:35,340
I'm sorry, this is all my fault.

152
00:08:35,340 --> 00:08:37,760
It's fine, I love cooking.

153
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:40,460
It's punishment for drawing on my face.

154
00:08:40,460 --> 00:08:41,800
You already apologized earlier, didn't you?

155
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:45,640
Now, now, let's all get along at mealtime.

156
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:46,580
Yeah, you're right.

157
00:08:47,420 --> 00:08:48,300
Thank you for the meal.

158
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:50,900
Wow, this is so good!

159
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:53,140
You'd make a good wife, you know.

160
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:54,140
Thank you very much.

161
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:58,220
Your mom sure is lively, isn't she?

162
00:08:58,220 --> 00:09:00,320
She's just very outgoing by nature.

163
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:03,080
She even takes on neighborhood
association duties on her own initiative.

164
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:07,060
I can't believe a mother like
that had a daughter as shy as Eve.

165
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:11,160
Eve wasn't that shy when she was little.

166
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:14,460
Then, when she was a child, an incident
Translation>
changed her.

167
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:16,140
What happened?

168
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:21,080
Once, I took Eve and Monkey
to Arakawa Amusement Park.

169
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:24,000
Arakawa Amusement Park,
what a blast from the past.

170
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,660
That place comes up a
lot in Ryo-chan's stories.

171
00:09:26,660 --> 00:09:28,740
I used to go there a
lot back in the day too.

172
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:32,560
Eve begged me to ride the Ferris wheel that time,
Translation>
so we got on it,

173
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:41,260
and then all of a sudden...

174
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:53,900
A 2B bomb was dropped on her from above.

175
00:09:54,580 --> 00:09:56,860
There are people who do such awful things.

176
00:09:57,940 --> 00:09:59,620
I vaguely remember it too.

177
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:01,740
Eve was completely terrified.

178
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:05,360
After that, she became
extremely reluctant to go outside.

179
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:09,320
As a result,
her personality became withdrawn as well.

180
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:15,700
I will never forgive the
person who dropped that 2B bomb.

181
00:10:15,700 --> 00:10:19,900
If only that guy hadn't been there, Eve
would have grown up cheerful and healthy.

182
00:10:19,900 --> 00:10:22,900
I understand how you feel.

183
00:10:22,900 --> 00:10:23,660
Senpai.

184
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:26,260
That story just now...

185
00:10:26,260 --> 00:10:28,000
It sounds like I've heard it somewhere.

186
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,500
Ryo-chan,
didn't you tell us a story like that before?

187
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:33,100
You said you threw a 2B
bomb from the Ferris wheel.

188
00:10:38,560 --> 00:10:41,920
Well, back then there were plenty
of people who did things like that.

189
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:45,960
Didn't they drop it on a
boy wearing a Nippon-Ham cap?

190
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:49,880
I was wearing a Nippon-Ham cap that day,
you know.

191
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:55,700
So the Nibee Gang back then was you, senpai?

192
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,040
Well, that's...

193
00:10:58,040 --> 00:11:00,380
So it was all your fault, senpai.

194
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:02,480
What are you going to do about it, senpai?

195
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:08,800
Well then, oh right, I'll go check on Eve.

196
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:09,960
I'm worried about her.

197
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:13,560
Leaving her alone with you,
senpai, is far more worrying.

198
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:15,663
Eve,

199
00:11:15,713 --> 00:11:20,020
Are you okay?

200
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:22,140
Looks like the fever came back.

201
00:11:22,560 --> 00:11:23,760
Her body's so frail.

202
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:26,180
Do you have any idea whose fault this is?

203
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:27,920
Eh, bachelor's degree?

204
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:29,300
It's hot.

205
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:31,020
Did you say it's hot, Eve?

206
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:36,140
Wait there, I'll bring ice right away.

207
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:37,700
Ice, ice!

208
00:11:40,980 --> 00:11:42,920
Is there anything else you want?

209
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:44,480
Water?

210
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:46,500
Got it, water it is.

211
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:49,100
Here's your water.

212
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:53,560
What a diligent girl.

213
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:55,240
He's really devoted to his little sister.

214
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:57,700
Is there anything else you want?

215
00:11:58,680 --> 00:11:59,640
A ring.

216
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:04,400
What about Corona, the kid, and Yuppi?

217
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:08,300
Corona's a kid...?

218
00:12:11,820 --> 00:12:13,080
Looks like she's fallen asleep.

219
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:18,280
Yupuu...

220
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:34,320
You've kept these so well, haven't you.

221
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:37,680
All of her childhood things
are stored right here.

222
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:42,460
Eve's childhood toys should
be in here somewhere, too.

223
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:46,660
Hey, these are Super Car erasers!

224
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:48,420
Don't tell me they've got every single kind.

225
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:51,380
Over here,
Rider Snacks with the candy still inside!

226
00:12:51,860 --> 00:12:54,260
Ryo-chan,
we didn't come here to play around!

227
00:12:54,260 --> 00:12:55,820
Look properly for the ring.

228
00:12:55,820 --> 00:12:57,780
Anyway,
who's to blame for Eve ending up like this?

229
00:12:57,780 --> 00:12:59,580
I know, I know.

230
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:02,760
Did you find it?

231
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:07,240
This is it, the hat the senpai
got hit with a Nibee pellet.

232
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,960
You don't need to show
me that kind of thing.

233
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:13,940
They even kept her diary?

234
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:17,380
Today Megumi-chan and I
made eye contact three times.

235
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:19,160
I was so happy.

236
00:13:20,060 --> 00:13:21,040
Please stop.

237
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:23,400
Reading someone else's
diary is in very bad taste.

238
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:26,480
Today I went to the
festival and bought a ring.

239
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:29,480
And I gave it to my little sister.

240
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:32,300
Isn't that about the ring?

241
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:37,800
I remember now.

242
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:46,620
I actually bought this ring
to give to a girl I liked.

243
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:51,760
But she flatly turned it down,
saying she didn't want it.

244
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:56,280
So I had no choice but to take it home,

245
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:59,780
and since Eve looked
like she really wanted it,

246
00:13:59,780 --> 00:14:01,480
I gave it to Eve.

247
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:08,840
Now that I think about it, she treasured
it like a precious gem for a while.

248
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:11,800
You don't know where it is now?

249
00:14:13,180 --> 00:14:14,200
Could it be...

250
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:16,500
Found it!

251
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:20,820
A while later, the three of us
siblings buried a time capsule.

252
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:23,700
We put everyone's treasures inside it.

253
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:25,060
The location is...

254
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:27,720
It's written right here.

255
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:33,640
Behind the municipal housing complex,

256
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:35,540
beside the forest,

257
00:14:36,280 --> 00:14:37,300
at the open field.

258
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:39,620
Yes, this is definitely the place.

259
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:45,920
This used to be the playground.

260
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:49,040
It's been completely
paved over with concrete.

261
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:51,060
Looks like we have no choice but to give up.

262
00:14:52,020 --> 00:14:52,480
No way.

263
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:53,180
No way...

264
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:55,740
Evie...

265
00:14:57,580 --> 00:14:58,260
Eve...

266
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:01,000
We can't give up!

267
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,600
Eve is waiting for us!

268
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:05,280
Let's go borrow some tools from over there!

269
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:06,980
And then, hey, hey, hey!

270
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:11,500
Isn't it here, then?

271
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:13,500
No, there's no mistake!

272
00:15:13,740 --> 00:15:15,620
It should be buried right here!

273
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:17,220
Senpai, don't get flustered!

274
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:18,520
Yeah, got it, okay.

275
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:20,440
Senpai! Honda-san!

276
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:22,080
Got it.

277
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:25,840
This ground was dug up when
they built the parking lot

278
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:28,120
and apparently it was
carted off to another site.

279
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:30,380
Which other site?

280
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:33,040
Apparently it's the one in Tama.

281
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:34,340
Tama?

282
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:37,800
They sure hauled it a long way.

283
00:15:38,540 --> 00:15:39,520
Tama

284
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:40,600
Hey, hey, hey.

285
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:42,100
Don't tell me, all the way to Tama?

286
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:44,720
Of course we're going to look for it.

287
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:46,720
Well, I'm going home, I'm not part of this.

288
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:48,720
Whose fault is this, Eve?

289
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:52,400
Alright, alright, I get it.

290
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:58,080
Mount Takao looks so close from here!

291
00:15:58,080 --> 00:16:01,180
Eve's university must
be over that way, right?

292
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:05,960
We've come all the way from Kameari, 50 kilometers.
We've really come a long way.

293
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:10,680
So the soil from the parking
lot was carried all the way here.

294
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:13,760
I can't say exactly where it is,

295
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:17,180
but it's probably being used as the
foundation for some building somewhere.

296
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:20,360
If it's come to this,
there's no way we can do anything about it.

297
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:21,880
I'm sorry,

298
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:24,460
but unfortunately we have
no choice but to give up.

299
00:16:24,460 --> 00:16:25,820
Well then, shall we get started?

300
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:29,320
Hey, weren't you listening
to what I just said?

301
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:31,520
It's probably under the foundations
of the buildings around here, right?

302
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:33,380
Then we'll just dig it all up.

303
00:16:34,220 --> 00:16:36,740
We'd have to dig up this entire area,
you know.

304
00:16:36,740 --> 00:16:38,480
Do you have any idea how
many days that would take?

305
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:39,500
Eve has been waiting.

306
00:16:39,980 --> 00:16:42,560
No matter how many days it takes,
we'll dig it up.

307
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:44,100
Days? You're kidding me.

308
00:16:44,980 --> 00:16:47,100
Nobody's blaming Eve.

309
00:16:47,100 --> 00:16:48,940
Fine, fine. I get it.

310
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:53,600
Isn't that Nakagawa's company over there?

311
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:57,460
Yes, we're extending our
subway line out to the suburbs.

312
00:16:57,460 --> 00:16:59,320
I see, this could be useful.

313
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:01,840
Honda, there's a better way than
digging with something like this.

314
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:03,420
Senpai, don't tell me...

315
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:06,320
We'll search from underground.

316
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:17,280
Could you lend us a hand?

317
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:21,020
President,
what brings you all the way out here?

318
00:17:21,020 --> 00:17:23,140
You have the latest
model tunnel cutter, right?

319
00:17:23,140 --> 00:17:24,920
We'd like to borrow it for a bit.

320
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:35,660
That thing should have a metal detector on it,
you know.

321
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:37,180
Alright!

322
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:42,700
Yes!

323
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:51,020
So that's how we pinpoint the capsule's location.
I see. It looks pretty easy to operate

324
00:17:51,020 --> 00:17:53,200
Aaaaah... well, whoa...

325
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:09,440
I'll give it back right away.

326
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:15,740
Aaaah, go ahead!

327
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:17,440
Time capsule

328
00:18:18,920 --> 00:18:21,800
Honda, there's a metal
reading to the upper right!

329
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:28,680
Right, keep going straight.

330
00:18:32,860 --> 00:18:36,380
Who cares about the water pipes!

331
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:47,400
This, this,
could it be Tokugawa's buried gold?

332
00:18:47,940 --> 00:18:49,420
Honda, stop!

333
00:18:49,780 --> 00:18:51,360
I've got no business with the police box!

334
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:52,420
Eve!

335
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:55,040
The police box!

336
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:03,120
There's something ahead!

337
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:12,620
Hang on, Eve.

338
00:19:12,620 --> 00:19:15,840
No matter what happens,
I'll definitely find it for you.

339
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:17,060
Eve!

340
00:19:17,060 --> 00:19:18,340
Eve!

341
00:19:18,340 --> 00:19:19,360
Eve!

342
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:20,500
Eve!

343
00:19:21,020 --> 00:19:23,980
Damn it, how about that time capsule?

344
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:51,060
Looks like your fever's
completely gone down.

345
00:19:51,060 --> 00:19:52,800
You're fine to get up now.

346
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:54,560
Sorry for the trouble.

347
00:19:58,320 --> 00:19:59,840
That big brother over there

348
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:02,100
has been searching for Eve's treasure.

349
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:08,160
This place...

350
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:09,160
You've been here before?

351
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:11,800
It's near my university's dormitory.

352
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:13,020
Look, over there.

353
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:15,460
So that's how it was.

354
00:20:20,520 --> 00:20:27,660
Big brother!

355
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:29,500
We finally found it, Eve!

356
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:30,400
This.

357
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:37,540
This is the time capsule
from when we were kids.

358
00:20:37,540 --> 00:20:41,360
You were delirious with fever the other day and kept talking about the ring,
remember?

359
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:45,340
Mr. Honda came all the
way out here to look for it.

360
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:47,000
Big brother.

361
00:20:48,660 --> 00:20:49,040
Yes.

362
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:56,600
Big brother gave me this ring.

363
00:21:06,740 --> 00:21:07,740
I'm not going in.

364
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:10,760
It means Eve has grown up too.

365
00:21:13,340 --> 00:21:15,760
Yeah, I have to grow up.

366
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:21,180
Big brother, I've made up my mind.

367
00:21:21,180 --> 00:21:23,500
I'm going to leave home
and live in a dormitory.

368
00:21:23,500 --> 00:21:25,740
Eve...

369
00:21:26,380 --> 00:21:28,000
I've been thinking about it for a while.

370
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:32,220
Once I'm in university, I want to get
over my shyness and become more dependable.

371
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:37,860
I figured living communally with lots of
people in a dorm would be good for that.

372
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:40,620
So that's why you chose
a university so far away.

373
00:21:41,260 --> 00:21:44,020
But when it came down to it,
I couldn't make up my mind.

374
00:21:44,820 --> 00:21:47,460
Thanks to you, big brother,
I finally made up my mind.

375
00:21:48,340 --> 00:21:50,500
That dormitory is my new home.

376
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:52,060
Eve...

377
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:53,800
What?

378
00:22:13,260 --> 00:22:14,660
Why would a herd like that

379
00:22:14,660 --> 00:22:17,120
come running out of the nearby Tama Zoo?

380
00:22:17,120 --> 00:22:20,200
Because you guys were
digging the ground like crazy!

381
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:21,580
It was Honda who dug it up!

382
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:26,380
It's coming this way, run!

383
00:22:31,140 --> 00:22:31,660
Run!

384
00:22:36,420 --> 00:22:39,220
Aaaaaah!

385
00:22:39,220 --> 00:22:40,960
Aaaaaah!

386
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:47,620
Saved! I was just put on its back.

387
00:22:48,420 --> 00:22:51,000
Hey, didn't you say your sister

388
00:22:51,360 --> 00:22:52,460
Yararararara!

389
00:22:59,020 --> 00:23:01,560
just like Honda goes wild
when he rides a motorcycle,

390
00:23:01,560 --> 00:23:04,460
she goes wild when she rides an elephant?

391
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:09,380
Stop messing with your pocket!
Let's go, you idiot!

392
00:23:13,740 --> 00:23:16,960
Ora ora ora ora! Let's go! Come on!

393
00:23:17,880 --> 00:23:20,220
I'm heading to Eve's university dorm!

394
00:23:22,460 --> 00:23:25,160
I'm moving into this dorm from now on!
Eve, for real!

395
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:26,980
I came to say hello!

396
00:23:45,820 --> 00:23:48,126
Ah ah ah ah ah ah

397
00:23:48,176 --> 00:23:50,714
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

398
00:23:50,764 --> 00:23:53,278
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

399
00:23:53,328 --> 00:23:55,891
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

400
00:23:55,941 --> 00:23:58,443
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

401
00:23:58,493 --> 00:24:01,044
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

402
00:24:01,094 --> 00:24:03,621
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

403
00:24:03,671 --> 00:24:06,340
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah, ah

404
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:13,980
First I draw my eyebrows,
then dash to the station, dash, dash, dash

405
00:24:13,980 --> 00:24:19,600
Main line train, a nap on Dad's back

406
00:24:20,620 --> 00:24:25,900
Another hard week,
and overwork is only to be expected

407
00:24:27,040 --> 00:24:33,300
Playing it cool with a bucket in hand,
but it's beef bowl with extra cloudy broth

408
00:24:33,300 --> 00:24:36,620
The frustration of endless overtime

409
00:24:36,620 --> 00:24:40,260
Melts away, frustration cleared out

410
00:24:43,620 --> 00:24:46,420
Every day is no problem,

411
00:24:46,420 --> 00:24:50,060
after a dip in a hot shower,

412
00:24:50,060 --> 00:24:53,020
every day is no problem,

413
00:24:53,020 --> 00:24:56,660
recharged with a restful sleep on a pillow.

414
00:24:59,860 --> 00:25:02,580
Every day is no problem,

415
00:25:03,360 --> 00:25:06,260
I love myself just like this.

416
00:25:06,260 --> 00:25:09,080
Every day is no play,

417
00:25:09,080 --> 00:25:13,060
hearts flying on a Monday.

418
00:25:13,060 --> 00:25:17,140
Mandeck mandeck program!

419
00:25:20,060 --> 00:25:23,320
Chief! Why are you stalking me?

420
00:25:23,700 --> 00:25:26,060
What on earth did I do?

421
00:25:26,260 --> 00:25:28,140
Please stop it, Chief!

422
00:25:28,480 --> 00:25:30,720
Chief! What's with that look?

423
00:25:30,800 --> 00:25:32,640
W-wait a minute, please!

424
00:25:33,540 --> 00:25:35,880
Next time on Chasing You, Kameari!

425
00:25:35,880 --> 00:25:36,820
Bu-ccha!

426
00:25:38,380 --> 00:25:39,020
Thank you.

